    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nDear CODEX2 Authors,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI would like to use your tool to call CNVs on WGS data. However, the tutorial only covers how to run the tool on WES data. Should the WGS data analyzed the same way as WES? or should the different recommendations be followed?</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nBest,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nMigle</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<hr>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"Gray\" size=\"1\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\nDenne e-mail indeholder fortrolig information. Hvis du ikke er den rette modtager af denne e-mail eller hvis du modtager den ved en fejltagelse, beder vi dig venligst informere afsender om fejlen ved at bruge svarfunktionen. Samtidig bedes du slette e-mailen\r\n med det samme uden at videresende eller kopiere den.<br>\r\n</font>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "2IhvtkSPAAAJ",
   "from": "Yuchao Jiang",
   "author": "94ec915e8ce36448",
   "date": "2019-05-14T03:46:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: [codex_wes_cnv] Running CODEX2 on WGS data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi Migle,<div><br></div><div>Yes CODEX2 is primarily for WES and targeted sequencing. For WGS, I think you can start with 5kb consecutive windows (the size depends on your sequencing depth but I think 5kb is a good start). That is, generate bed file with each row corresponding to a 5kb window along the genome.</div><div><br></div><div>Hope that this helps,</div><div>Yuchao</div><div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On May 13, 2019, at 11:00 PM, Migle Gabrielaite &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">migle.ga...@regionh.dk</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
